<!DOCTYPE html>

<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:wght@700&family=Lato:wght@300;400;700&family=Dancing+Script:wght@600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root{
    --charcoal:#2D2D2D; --near-black:#1C1C1E; --yellow:#E8C547; --yellow-pale:#FBF5DA;
    --pink:#E89BB5; --pink-pale:#F9EFF4; --off-white:#FFFDF9; --white:#FFFFFF;
    --muted:#6B7A68; --light-muted:#9DADA6;
  }
  *{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box;}
  .slide{
    width:1080px;height:1440px;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;position:relative;overflow:hidden;
  }
  /* Photo background bleeds full-frame on every slide */
  .photo-bg{position:absolute;inset:0;background-image:url("data:image/jpeg;base64,");
    background-size:cover;background-position:center 30%;z-index:0;}
  /* Charcoal scrim so text stays readable over the photo */
  .scrim{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:1;
    background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(45,45,45,0.82) 0%, rgba(45,45,45,0.55) 42%, rgba(45,45,45,0.35) 62%, rgba(45,45,45,0.78) 100%);}
  .scrim-heavy{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:1;background:rgba(45,45,45,0.86);}
  .safe{
    position:absolute;top:180px;right:120px;bottom:180px;left:50px;z-index:2;
    display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;
  }
  .safe.safe-top{justify-content:flex-start;}
  .headline{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-weight:700;line-height:1.12;color:var(--off-white);}
  .hook{font-size:82px;}
  .h-slide{font-size:60px;}
  .body{font-size:36px;line-height:1.4;font-weight:400;margin-top:32px;color:var(--off-white);}
  .caption-dark{font-size:26px;color:var(--light-muted);font-weight:400;}
  .creds{font-family:'Dancing Script',cursive;font-size:34px;}
  .script-word{font-family:'Dancing Script',cursive;font-weight:600;color:var(--pink);}
  .highlight-yellow{color:var(--yellow);}
  .highlight-pink{color:var(--pink);}
  .swipe-yellow{background:var(--yellow);color:var(--charcoal);padding:4px 18px;border-radius:6px 14px 8px 16px;box-decoration-break:clone;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;}
  .swipe-pink{background:var(--pink);color:var(--charcoal);padding:4px 18px;border-radius:6px 14px 8px 16px;box-decoration-break:clone;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;}
  .underline-pink{border-bottom:8px solid var(--pink);padding-bottom:2px;}
  .underline-yellow{border-bottom:8px solid var(--yellow);padding-bottom:2px;}
  .accent-bar{width:120px;height:10px;background:var(--yellow);margin-bottom:40px;}
  .counter{position:absolute;top:80px;left:50px;background:var(--pink);color:var(--charcoal);
    font-family:'Lato';font-weight:700;font-size:32px;padding:10px 28px;border-radius:40px;z-index:3;}
  /* Listicle number badge, the reference look */
  .num{font-family:'Lato';font-weight:700;font-size:40px;color:var(--yellow);margin-bottom:6px;letter-spacing:1px;}
  .item-head{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-weight:700;font-size:66px;line-height:1.08;color:var(--off-white);}
  .item-sub{font-size:34px;line-height:1.4;font-weight:400;margin-top:24px;color:var(--off-white);max-width:840px;}
  .caption-page{background:var(--off-white);color:var(--charcoal);padding:120px 90px;
    display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-start;}
  .caption-flag{font-family:'Lato';font-weight:700;font-size:28px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--pink);margin-bottom:40px;}
  .caption-body{font-family:'Lato';font-weight:400;font-size:36px;line-height:1.5;white-space:pre-wrap;}
  .caption-tags{font-family:'Lato';font-weight:700;font-size:34px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:40px;}
  .caption-accounts{font-family:'Lato';font-weight:400;font-size:30px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:28px;}
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Slide 1: Hook -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="Hook"
       data-speaker-notes="Photo background. Text pinned top over the scrim. Add a doodle arrow or sparkle near the hook in Canva if you want.">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim"></div>
    <div class="counter">1/7</div>
    <div class="safe safe-top">
      <div class="accent-bar"></div>
      <h1 class="headline hook">5 ways to make haircuts <span class="script-word">easier</span> for your sensitive kid</h1>
      <p class="body">Without the tears.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide 2: Item 1 -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="1 - Prep the story">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim"></div>
    <div class="counter">2/7</div>
    <div class="safe">
      <div class="num">001</div>
      <h2 class="item-head">Prep the story first</h2>
      <p class="item-sub">Walk them through exactly what will happen before you ever leave the house. Sensitive kids settle when there are no surprises waiting.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide 3: Item 2 -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="2 - Meet the tools">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim"></div>
    <div class="counter">3/7</div>
    <div class="safe">
      <div class="num">002</div>
      <h2 class="item-head">Let them meet the tools</h2>
      <p class="item-sub">Ask the stylist to let them hold the clippers, feel the cape, hear the buzz before anything starts. A minute of getting familiar takes away the startle.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide 4: Item 3 -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="3 - Quiet slot">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim"></div>
    <div class="counter">4/7</div>
    <div class="safe">
      <div class="num">003</div>
      <h2 class="item-head">Book the quiet slot</h2>
      <p class="item-sub">First appointment of the day or right after opening. Fewer people, less noise, no waiting room buzz building up in their body.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide 5: Item 4 -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="4 - Comfort anchor">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim"></div>
    <div class="counter">5/7</div>
    <div class="safe">
      <div class="num">004</div>
      <h2 class="item-head">Bring the comfort anchor</h2>
      <p class="item-sub">A favorite toy, a fidget, a snack, a lollipop. One familiar thing in their hands gives their nervous system something to hold onto.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide 6: Item 5 -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="5 - Name the finish line">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim"></div>
    <div class="counter">6/7</div>
    <div class="safe">
      <div class="num">005</div>
      <h2 class="item-head">Name the finish line</h2>
      <p class="item-sub">Tell them what happens after and how long it will take. "Three songs and we're done" gives a sensitive kid an ending to reach for.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide 7: CTA -->

  <div class="slide" data-document-role="page" data-label="CTA">
    <div class="photo-bg"></div>
    <div class="scrim-heavy"></div>
    <div class="counter">7/7</div>
    <div class="safe">
      <h2 class="headline h-slide">Want the full playbook?</h2>
      <p class="body">Comment <span class="swipe-yellow">HAIR</span> and I'll send you my free guide to haircuts with sensitive kids.</p>
      <p class="body">Follow <span class="highlight-yellow">@as_the_littles_grow</span> for more.</p>
      <p class="creds" style="margin-top:40px;color:var(--light-muted);">Speech Pathologist + Highly Sensitive Person + Homeschooling Mom of 4</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Caption page (copy/paste, not for posting) -->

  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Haircuts can undo a sensitive kid before the first snip. It is not the haircut they are fighting. It is the buzzing, the cape on their neck, the stranger too close, the not knowing when it ends.

Here are 5 small things that make the whole thing softer. None of them change your kid. They just give their nervous system a little more to hold onto.

Which one are you trying first?

Comment HAIR and I will send you my free guide to haircuts with sensitive kids.</div>
<div class="caption-tags">#sensitivekids #HSC #gentleparenting</div>
<div class="caption-accounts">Tag: none needed</div>

  </div>

</body>
</html>
